 "text": "9/29/26, 10:15 AM\n\nDisplaying and Changing Installment Plans\n\nTo view or change existing installment agreements for a business partner, proceed as follows:\n\n1. In the SAP Easy Access screen, choose |)Account\n\n2. Choose Change or Display.\n\n3. Specify the desired installment plan and choose Continue.\n\n1 Note\n\nInstallment Plan >\u00bb Display 3 (transaction FPR3).\n\nIf you use the input help for the Installment Plan Number field, for selection using the installment plan history, the\nsystem displays only active installment plans as standard. If you also want to display deactivated installment plans, you\n\nhave to specify a deactivation reason on the tab page Installment Plan History.\n\nThe following table lists the functions you can use when changing or displaying an installment plan:\n\nFunctions with Display and Change\n\nPrint letter\n\nDisplay source receivables in the account\nbalance display\n\nDisplay installment plan changes\n\nDisplay interest supplement\n\nDisplay / change processing locks\n\nCalling the function\n\nInstallment Plan Save + Create Letter\n\nEnvironment \u00bb Source Receivable\n(Account Display)\n\nGoto } Changes\n\nEnvironment > Interest Supplement\n\nThe system will display locks, such as\n\npayment, dunning, interest, and clearing\nlocks, together for each installment plan\n\nitem. When you place the cursor on the icon\n(3; the type of locks that exist are\ndisplayed in a quick info. For detailed\ninformation, such as the lock reason,\n\ndouble-click on the icon and select the\nrequired lock in the following dialog box.\n\nThe overview also shows a column for each\nprocessing lock with the relevant lock\nreason. If there are several locks of the\nsame type with different lock reasons, a\ntilde appears (~). By double-clicking on the\ntable field with the lock required, you can\n\nricnlarys ann nhbaAnnn than Antaile far thic lAnL\n\nProcedure / Notes\n\nThe letter is written into the\ncorrespondence container. For more\ninformation on output, see Functions for\nScheduling Program Runs, Printing\n\nCorrespondence, and Printing\nCorrespondence with the Print Workbench.\n\nThe system calls up the account balance\ndisplay. You see the documents that were\n\ntransferred to installment plan.\n\nThe precondition is that interest was\ncharged on the installment plan.\n\nTo set or change a lock, navigate using the\nicon 4 or by double-clicking on the\ncorresponding table field in the overview to\nthe dialog box for setting/changing the\nrequired lock and enter the data required.\n\nAlternatively, delete the lock reason or\nenter it in the required column in the\noverview. The field is only ready for input if\n\nonly one unlimited lock exists or if there are\nnone.\n\nIn this way, you can only set time-based\nunlimited locks.\n",
